<title>UK: Kwiksave slides on market share woes.</title>
<headline>Kwiksave slides on market share woes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kwiksave Group Plc continued their downward spiral on growing concern Safeway Plc and other major UK supermarket chains were winning market share, dealers and analysts said.</p>
<p>Annual results from Safeway which showed an improvement in sales reinforced the view that Safeway and others were benefitting at Kwiksave's expense, they said.</p>
<p>By 1314 GMT, Kwiksave shares were down 13p to 267-1/2.</p>
<p>Shares in Safeway jumped 20p to 351.</p>
<p>Among shares in other big grocers, Tesco Plc added 5p to 385, having scored a new peak at 386p earlier.</p>
<p>But shares in ASDA Group slipped one penny to 118-1/2, while shares in J. Sainsbury fell 1/2p to 377-1/2.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
